  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "68c3443b9a0fdf43:1",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "68c3443b9a0fdf43_GENERATION_TIMELINES.md",
      "text": "Generation and prompt timelines are distinct: the first records prepared and generated work, while the second records evolving human instructions. Real program state has its own execution timeline.",
      "relevance": 0.333,
      "source_sha256": "68c3443b9a0fdf43bca5bec4747b3356b99336b0e61fbc9b7a56a69ebd57b44d",
      "tick": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "68c3443b9a0fdf43:2",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "68c3443b9a0fdf43_GENERATION_TIMELINES.md",
      "text": "Generation branches appear as tabs connected to one generation job rather than three disconnected main timelines. A proposal may be staged before the user supplies additional conditions.",
      "relevance": 0.167,
      "source_sha256": "68c3443b9a0fdf43bca5bec4747b3356b99336b0e61fbc9b7a56a69ebd57b44d",
      "tick": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6f77d75a686cc1a6:1",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "6f77d75a686cc1a6_PROBE_NETWORK.md",
      "text": "An agent research probe should launch because it addresses a specific evidence gap, independent question or contradiction, not merely because a model produced interesting prose.",
      "relevance": 0.167,
      "source_sha256": "6f77d75a686cc1a62147d1a5c90688b7b3ce9b25ed01137c10597b920a86af8e",
      "tick": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6f77d75a686cc1a6:2",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "6f77d75a686cc1a6_PROBE_NETWORK.md",
      "text": "Budget allocation should account for observed evidence gain, user focus, cost and diminishing returns. Unverified model proposals must not be scored as evidence.",
      "relevance": 0.167,
      "source_sha256": "6f77d75a686cc1a62147d1a5c90688b7b3ce9b25ed01137c10597b920a86af8e",
      "tick": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "accf800b37d8ff9d:1",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "accf800b37d8ff9d_SIGNAL_SPINE_REFERENCE.md",
      "text": "A MIDI event is a symbolic message describing note or controller data. MIDI is not an acoustic recording and MIDI event timings are not inherently model thinking speed.",
      "relevance": 0.167,
      "source_sha256": "accf800b37d8ff9d30f9df825b8b87192c15249a3805d6602ea9c5565ec36b72",
      "tick": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "accf800b37d8ff9d:2",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "accf800b37d8ff9d_SIGNAL_SPINE_REFERENCE.md",
      "text": "A DAW edits time-addressed media. Tracks, clips and routing do not require replacing the sound engine when the selected visual facade changes.",
      "relevance": 0.167,
      "source_sha256": "accf800b37d8ff9d30f9df825b8b87192c15249a3805d6602ea9c5565ec36b72",
      "tick": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "accf800b37d8ff9d:3",
      "branch": "p001",
      "file": "accf800b37d8ff9d_SIGNAL_SPINE_REFERENCE.md",
      "text": "The FocusGate M0.2 prototype recorded 56 consecutively numbered simulated ticks during facade switching, a staged capability promotion and rollback. This is a software continuity test, not a claim of real-time MIDI timing.",
      "relevance": 0.5,
      "source_sha256": "accf800b37d8ff9d30f9df825b8b87192c15249a3805d6602ea9c5565ec36b72",
      "tick": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "6f77d75a686cc1a6:3",
      "branch": "p003",
      "file": "6f77d75a686cc1a6_PROBE_NETWORK.md",
      "text": "Dormant agent branches can be parked with their state retained. New relevant evidence may trigger a bounded reactivation, with loop limits to avoid expensive repeated work.",
      "relevance": 0.444,
      "source_sha256": "6f77d75a686cc1a62147d1a5c90688b7b3ce9b25ed01137c10597b920a86af8e",
      "tick": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "accf800b37d8ff9d:4",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "accf800b37d8ff9d_SIGNAL_SPINE_REFERENCE.md",
      "text": "GHOSTFIELD remains a proposed independent MIDI service for Linux. Its port stability, Note On/Off and CC16 readback into REAPER need physical host verification.",
      "relevance": 0.167,
      "source_sha256": "accf800b37d8ff9d30f9df825b8b87192c15249a3805d6602ea9c5565ec36b72",
      "tick": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "68c3443b9a0fdf43:3",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "68c3443b9a0fdf43_GENERATION_TIMELINES.md",
      "text": "A prompt can arrive after computation has started. Only future, not-yet-committed work can use that prompt without rollback or regeneration. Processing latency is a scheduling opportunity but not a reason to add artificial lag.",
      "relevance": 0.083,
      "source_sha256": "68c3443b9a0fdf43bca5bec4747b3356b99336b0e61fbc9b7a56a69ebd57b44d",
      "tick": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "6f77d75a686cc1a6:5",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "6f77d75a686cc1a6_PROBE_NETWORK.md",
      "text": "The primary goal remains addressable while its research branches grow and contract. Only one session state owner should commit the event ledger.",
      "relevance": 0.095,
      "source_sha256": "6f77d75a686cc1a62147d1a5c90688b7b3ce9b25ed01137c10597b920a86af8e",
      "tick": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "68c3443b9a0fdf43:4",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "68c3443b9a0fdf43_GENERATION_TIMELINES.md",
      "text": "Prompt revisions may specify new targets, corrections, constraints, or ambiguous partial ideas. Ambiguous speech cannot be assumed to authorize executable system actions.",
      "relevance": 0.048,
      "source_sha256": "68c3443b9a0fdf43bca5bec4747b3356b99336b0e61fbc9b7a56a69ebd57b44d",
      "tick": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "accf800b37d8ff9d:0",
      "branch": "root",
      "file": "accf800b37d8ff9d_SIGNAL_SPINE_REFERENCE.md",
      "text": "# FlowMesh acceptance corpus / sourced from the prior local FocusGate architecture",
